WEBVTT

00:00:11.846 --> 00:00:16.730
The Lost Treasure of Bodega Bay by Gina D.B.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:17.710
Clement.

00:00:17.771 --> 00:00:26.824
Copyright Black Cat Publishing.

00:00:26.883 --> 00:00:38.900
Introduction This story takes place in San Francisco and in Bodega Bay.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:44.654
San Francisco is a beautiful city on the Pacific coast in the state of California.

00:00:44.714 --> 00:00:50.644
Bodega Bay is a small town on the coast, north of San Francisco.

00:00:50.704 --> 00:01:07.635
The story talks about a big marine sanctuary called the Gulf of the Farrelones National Marine Sanctuary, 27 miles west of San Francisco, and the Point Reyes National Seashore, which is another protected area.

00:01:07.695 --> 00:01:10.060
San Francisco.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:15.468
San Francisco is one of America's most beautiful and exciting cities.

00:01:15.528 --> 00:01:21.264
It is an international center for business, education, science, and the arts.

00:01:21.324 --> 00:01:23.968
The city is famous for its hills.

00:01:24.028 --> 00:01:29.594
It was built on 43 hills, and you can always get great views of the bay.

00:01:29.654 --> 00:01:37.566
The main tourist attractions are the Golden Gate Bridge, Alcatraz Island, Telegraph Hill and Fisherman's Wharf.

00:01:37.626 --> 00:01:42.086
Around 800,000 people live in the city today.

00:01:42.146 --> 00:01:56.600
The Farrelones National Marine Sanctuary and Point Rays The Farrelones National Marine Sanctuary is one of the 13 marine sanctuaries in the United States.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:02:06.006
There are seven groups of islands, and it is home to whales, dolphins, great white sharks, sea lions, and seabirds.

00:02:06.066 --> 00:02:11.220
Tourists can't go onto the islands, but they can see them from boats.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:14.910
Only scientists can go on the islands.

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:21.442
Point Ray's National Seashore is part of the Feralones National Marine Sanctuary.

00:02:21.502 --> 00:02:28.486
It was set up in 1962 to protect all kinds of sea life, plants and trees.

00:02:28.546 --> 00:02:35.450
Visitors can walk along the Long Beach and watch whales and dolphins swim by.

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:38.110
Bodega Bay.

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:45.386
Bodega Bay is a small town on the Pacific coast, about 40 miles northwest of San Francisco.

00:02:45.446 --> 00:02:54.513
The bay was discovered in 1775 by Peruvian explorer Juan Francisco de la Bodega Ijhadra.

00:02:54.573 --> 00:02:58.285
About 2,000 people lived there today.

00:02:58.345 --> 00:03:04.088
The town was the setting for Alfred Hitchcock's film The Birds in 1963.

00:03:04.148 --> 00:03:11.067
It is well known for its long sandy beaches and its protected harbor.

00:03:11.127 --> 00:03:24.580
Chapter 1 The Story of the Ghost Ship Kate and Mike Sullivan live in San Francisco with their parents and their pet dog Lucky.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:34.264
Their home is on Russian Hill, and from their house Kate and Mike have a great view of San Francisco Bay and the Golden Gate Bridge.

00:03:34.324 --> 00:03:41.660
Their father, Frank Sullivan, is a professor and teaches marine biology at San Francisco University.

00:03:41.719 --> 00:03:47.132
Their mother, Liz Sullivan, works in a big bookshop in the city center.

00:03:47.192 --> 00:03:52.043
Kate is 14, and her brother Mike is 15.

00:03:52.103 --> 00:03:58.174
Kate goes to Lincoln Middle School, and Mike goes to Galileo High School.

00:03:58.234 --> 00:04:03.276
Kate is a pretty girl with long blonde hair and blue eyes.

00:04:03.336 --> 00:04:06.497
She likes school, but doesn't like math.

00:04:06.557 --> 00:04:10.661
She loves dancing and belongs to the Lincoln Dance Club.

00:04:10.721 --> 00:04:15.838
She's a very good dancer and wants to become a professional dancer one day.

00:04:15.898 --> 00:04:20.212
Mike is tall with brown hair and blue eyes.

00:04:20.272 --> 00:04:25.336
He is in his first year of high school and he always has a lot of homework.

00:04:25.396 --> 00:04:31.652
He is an excellent swimmer and is a member of the Galileo High School swimming team.

00:04:31.712 --> 00:04:36.516
Our story begins on a sunny Monday morning early in June.

00:04:36.536 --> 00:04:38.975
Half past seven.

00:04:39.035 --> 00:04:41.283
Said Kate, putting on her watch.

00:04:41.343 --> 00:04:42.794
Time for breakfast.

00:04:42.854 --> 00:04:45.546
Two more weeks and school is over.

00:04:45.606 --> 00:04:47.096
Said Mike, happily.

00:04:47.156 --> 00:04:50.508
Summer vacation, the best time of the year.

00:04:50.568 --> 00:04:52.739
Said Kate, laughing.

00:04:52.799 --> 00:04:58.412
Kate was also excited because after the summer, she was going to start high school.

00:04:58.472 --> 00:05:00.283
Good morning.

00:05:00.343 --> 00:05:03.485
Said Mrs. Sullivan, who was preparing breakfast.

00:05:03.545 --> 00:05:09.080
Kate, remember you have an eye doctor's appointment today after school with Dr. Lee?

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:10.672
Please don't be late.

00:05:10.732 --> 00:05:11.954
I know, Mom.

00:05:12.014 --> 00:05:13.194
Said Kate.

00:05:13.254 --> 00:05:14.676
But I don't want to go.

00:05:14.696 --> 00:05:17.028
I don't want to wear glasses.

00:05:17.088 --> 00:05:20.102
Kate, you can't study well at school.

00:05:20.162 --> 00:05:21.994
You need a pair of glasses.

00:05:22.054 --> 00:05:25.496
If you don't get them, your eyesight will get worse.

00:05:25.556 --> 00:05:28.880
Said Mr. Sullivan, drinking a cup of coffee.

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:31.333
There's nothing wrong with glasses.

00:05:31.392 --> 00:05:32.294
I wear them.

00:05:32.354 --> 00:05:33.954
A lot of kids wear them.

00:05:34.013 --> 00:05:37.433
Susan Garcia in my class just got glasses.

00:05:37.493 --> 00:05:38.573
Said Mike.

00:05:38.633 --> 00:05:42.024
And she looks better with glasses than without them.

00:05:42.084 --> 00:05:45.714
Kate slowly ate her breakfast and said.

00:05:45.774 --> 00:05:47.744
Okay, okay.

00:05:47.804 --> 00:05:49.945
I'll wear them to see the board.

00:05:50.005 --> 00:05:52.735
Suddenly there was a knock on the door.

00:05:52.795 --> 00:05:55.816
It was Julie Bennett, Kate's best friend.

00:05:55.876 --> 00:05:56.966
Hi.

00:05:57.026 --> 00:06:01.790
Said Julie, a pretty 14 year old girl with short black hair.

00:06:01.850 --> 00:06:04.883
I came to pick you up so we can walk to school together.

00:06:04.903 --> 00:06:06.214
Hi, Julie.

00:06:06.274 --> 00:06:07.314
Said Kate.

00:06:07.374 --> 00:06:09.165
I'm still having breakfast.

00:06:09.225 --> 00:06:11.416
Just sit down and have some cookies.

00:06:11.476 --> 00:06:13.017
Hi, Julie.

00:06:13.077 --> 00:06:19.260
Said Mrs. Sullivan as she turned on the television to watch the weather report and the morning news.

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:22.936
Another warm sunny day in San Francisco.

00:06:22.996 --> 00:06:24.340
said the speaker.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:30.494
With heavy afternoon fog along the Pacific coast, particularly in the Bodega Bay area.

00:06:30.554 --> 00:06:33.796
It's always foggy in Bodega Bay.

00:06:33.856 --> 00:06:34.958
Said Mike.

00:06:35.018 --> 00:06:37.620
Do you remember our adventure up there?

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:40.272
When did you go to Bodega Bay?

00:06:40.332 --> 00:06:42.714
Ask Julie, eating a cookie.

00:06:42.774 --> 00:06:45.176
It was about eighteen months ago.

00:06:45.236 --> 00:06:46.356
Said Kate.

00:06:46.416 --> 00:06:48.437
And Carlos Gomez came with us.

00:06:48.497 --> 00:06:50.748
We had quite an adventure.

00:06:50.808 --> 00:06:52.488
Sounds exciting.

00:06:52.548 --> 00:06:53.749
Said Julie.

00:06:53.809 --> 00:06:55.440
Tell me about it.

00:06:55.499 --> 00:06:58.340
Kate looked at Mike and her parents.

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:00.761
And they all started laughing.

00:07:00.821 --> 00:07:04.122
Well, Mom and I have to go to work.

00:07:04.182 --> 00:07:05.553
Said Mr. Sullivan.

00:07:05.613 --> 00:07:06.833
It's getting late.

00:07:06.893 --> 00:07:08.064
See you this evening.

00:07:08.124 --> 00:07:08.934
Bye.

00:07:08.994 --> 00:07:11.656
Okay, let me tell you about it.

00:07:11.716 --> 00:07:14.278
Said Kate, looking at her watch.

00:07:14.338 --> 00:07:21.139
Mom, Dad, Mike, Carlos, and I went to the Fairlawn Islands on Dad's new boat, the Pelican.

00:07:21.199 --> 00:07:24.470
He was studying the seabirds and the fish in the area.

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:30.762
We were all excited about the trip, but the first night I saw the ghost of a boy near my bed.

00:07:30.822 --> 00:07:34.573
I screamed and was scared, but no one believed me.

00:07:34.633 --> 00:07:40.136
Then one night Mom and Dad heard a ship's bell and saw a yellow light at sea.

00:07:40.196 --> 00:07:45.309
They thought someone needed help, so they took the lifeboat and left the Pelican.

00:07:45.368 --> 00:07:49.391
The next morning we couldn't find them and we were worried.

00:07:49.451 --> 00:07:52.302
We took the boat and went to look for them.

00:07:52.362 --> 00:07:56.905
In the fog we saw a strange old ship, the Sonora.

00:07:56.965 --> 00:08:04.308
Later, we discovered that it was an old Spanish pirate ship that was lost at sea in 1608.

00:08:04.368 --> 00:08:05.188
What?

00:08:05.248 --> 00:08:08.600
A ship that was lost 400 years ago?

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:11.131
Cried Julie, who stopped eating.

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:13.662
Yes, it was a ghost ship.

00:08:13.722 --> 00:08:14.820
Said Kate.

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:19.529
We knew Mom and Dad were on that ship because their lifeboat was there.

00:08:19.589 --> 00:08:25.081
We were scared, but we went onto the ship and we had a terrible surprise.

00:08:25.141 --> 00:08:28.002
The ship's crew were all ghosts.

00:08:28.062 --> 00:08:30.383
Ghosts of sailors and pirates.

00:08:30.443 --> 00:08:34.975
We were terrified because we saw Mom and Dad sitting in a corner.

00:08:35.035 --> 00:08:40.282
We went to help them, but then the ghost of Captain Salamanca spoke to us.

00:08:40.342 --> 00:08:41.874
He was terrible.

00:08:41.934 --> 00:08:46.500
He killed people and they became part of his crew of ghosts.

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:51.836
He said he needed a big crew because he was looking for some lost treasure.

00:08:51.896 --> 00:08:54.258
He wanted to kill us all!

00:08:54.318 --> 00:09:00.534
Suddenly, Lucky jumped on the table and a big candle fell and a fire started.

00:09:00.594 --> 00:09:06.619
Ghosts are afraid of fire, so they moved away and we helped Mom and Dad get off the ship.

00:09:06.679 --> 00:09:12.353
Before leaving, Mike saw Captain Salamanca's treasure map on the table and took it.

00:09:12.414 --> 00:09:14.936
What an adventure!

00:09:14.996 --> 00:09:16.427
Said Julie.

00:09:16.487 --> 00:09:18.829
But you still have the treasure map?

00:09:18.889 --> 00:09:20.100
Mike has it.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:21.112
Said Kate.

00:09:21.172 --> 00:09:24.365
But he hit it because it's a big secret.

00:09:24.425 --> 00:09:28.810
That afternoon, Kate went to the eye doctor with Julie.

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:31.924
Dr. Lee was a friendly young man.

00:09:31.983 --> 00:09:38.654
He gave her an eye test and said, Kate, you need glasses to see things in the distance.

00:09:38.714 --> 00:09:46.119
Julie helped Kate choose her new glasses, and she gave them to Dr. Lee, who said, Good choice.

00:09:46.179 --> 00:09:50.320
They'll be ready on Thursday, Kate.

00:09:50.380 --> 00:10:02.502
Chapter 2 A New Adventure Friday was a big day for Kate, because she wore her new glasses to school for the first time.

00:10:02.562 --> 00:10:07.392
When she walked into the classroom, everyone turned around and looked at her.

00:10:07.452 --> 00:10:09.142
Wow!

00:10:09.202 --> 00:10:10.013
They said.

00:10:10.033 --> 00:10:12.704
New glasses!

00:10:12.764 --> 00:10:17.506
Kate's heart was beating fast and her hands felt cold.

00:10:17.566 --> 00:10:20.477
She walked to her desk and sat down.

00:10:20.537 --> 00:10:21.868
Hi, Kate!

00:10:21.928 --> 00:10:24.669
Said Tom, the boy she liked.

00:10:24.729 --> 00:10:26.100
New glasses?

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:27.500
You look great.

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:28.850
Thanks, Tom.

00:10:28.910 --> 00:10:32.162
Said Kate, turning red with embarrassment.

00:10:32.222 --> 00:10:35.356
His opinion was very important to her.

00:10:35.416 --> 00:10:40.310
I really like your new glasses," said her friend Kelly.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:46.454
Kate suddenly felt happy and was ready for the lesson, a math test.

00:10:46.514 --> 00:10:54.477
That evening at the dinner table, the Sullivan family was having a noisy conversation because everyone had something to say.

00:10:54.537 --> 00:10:57.458
Well, how was your day at school, Kate?

00:10:57.518 --> 00:10:58.769
Asked her mother.

00:10:58.829 --> 00:11:00.620
Oh, just great, Mom.

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:02.272
Said Kate, smiling.

00:11:02.332 --> 00:11:08.525
Everyone liked my new glasses, even Tom, and the math test was okay, I think.

00:11:08.585 --> 00:11:10.466
And how was your day, Mike?

00:11:10.526 --> 00:11:11.736
Asked his father.

00:11:11.796 --> 00:11:13.027
Exciting.

00:11:13.087 --> 00:11:14.177
Mike said.

00:11:14.237 --> 00:11:15.358
Guess what?

00:11:15.418 --> 00:11:19.920
Our science class is going to Muir Woods National Park next week.

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:24.782
It's part of a class project on trees, forests, and conservation.

00:11:24.842 --> 00:11:29.604
We're leaving early on Tuesday morning and coming back before dinner time.

00:11:29.664 --> 00:11:31.134
Muir Woods.

00:11:31.194 --> 00:11:32.623
Said Mrs. Sullivan.

00:11:32.683 --> 00:11:36.355
It's one of the most beautiful forests in the world.

00:11:36.415 --> 00:11:37.885
Sounds like fun.

00:11:37.945 --> 00:11:39.296
Said Kate.

00:11:39.356 --> 00:11:43.377
Well, this evening I have some exciting news too.

00:11:43.437 --> 00:11:45.208
Said Mr. Sullivan.

00:11:45.268 --> 00:11:47.618
Everyone at the table looked at him.

00:11:47.678 --> 00:11:50.850
He usually didn't have anything exciting to say.

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:52.528
What is it, Frank?

00:11:52.588 --> 00:11:55.769
Said Mrs. Sullivan, who wanted to know the news.

00:11:55.829 --> 00:12:01.453
Next week, I'm going to the Monterey Bay Aquarium to talk to Professor Simpson.

00:12:01.513 --> 00:12:02.974
Said Mr. Sullivan.

00:12:03.034 --> 00:12:10.219
The aquarium is doing an important study on sea life in the Pacific Ocean, particularly on the Great White Shark.

00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:16.044
They want me to spend some time at the Farallon Islands and the Point Reyes National Seashore.

00:12:16.103 --> 00:12:18.896
Another trip to the Farallon Islands.

00:12:18.956 --> 00:12:21.061
Said his wife, smiling.

00:12:21.121 --> 00:12:26.940
Wow, Dad, do you mean you're going to the fair lawns and point rays on the pelican?"

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:29.401
asked Mike, looking at Kate.

00:12:29.461 --> 00:12:32.744
Yes, that's right, said Mr. Sullivan.

00:12:32.804 --> 00:12:37.588
I'll probably stay about a week and more the pelican in the harbor at Bodega Bay.

00:12:37.648 --> 00:12:39.038
When are you going?

00:12:39.098 --> 00:12:41.150
asked Kate excitedly.

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:45.564
At the end of June, or the beginning of July, said Mr. Sullivan.

00:12:45.624 --> 00:12:47.160
Can we come along?

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:48.895
cried Kate and Mike.

00:12:48.955 --> 00:12:50.466
Of course!

00:12:50.526 --> 00:12:52.447
said Mr. Sullivan, laughing.

00:12:52.507 --> 00:12:53.808
What about Lucky?

00:12:53.868 --> 00:12:55.449
asked Kate.

00:12:55.508 --> 00:12:59.531
Lucky heard his name and started barking.

00:12:59.591 --> 00:13:02.553
Yes, Lucky can come too.

00:13:02.613 --> 00:13:04.194
Said Mr. Sullivan.

00:13:04.254 --> 00:13:07.286
Ah, it'll be great fun like last time.

00:13:07.346 --> 00:13:08.236
Said Mike.

00:13:08.296 --> 00:13:10.107
But without the ghosts.

00:13:10.167 --> 00:13:11.748
Said Kate nervously.

00:13:11.808 --> 00:13:15.572
Yes, without the ghosts and the ghost ship.

00:13:15.632 --> 00:13:20.318
said Mrs. Sullivan, who still remembered that terrible adventure.

00:13:20.378 --> 00:13:24.360
Oh, Dad, can we invite Carlos like last time?

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:25.922
asked Mike.

00:13:25.982 --> 00:13:29.224
Carlos Gomez was Mike's best friend.

00:13:29.284 --> 00:13:33.856
He was his Spano-American, and he spoke Spanish and English perfectly.

00:13:33.916 --> 00:13:40.570
He was a tall, friendly boy with short black hair and dark eyes, and he lived near the Sullivan's.

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:41.852
Why not?

00:13:41.912 --> 00:13:44.562
said Mr. Sullivan, smiling at his son.

00:13:44.622 --> 00:13:45.883
Thanks, Dad!"

00:13:45.943 --> 00:13:50.086
cried Mike, who started making secret plans.

00:13:50.146 --> 00:13:54.128
Kate and Mike helped their parents clean up after dinner.

00:13:54.188 --> 00:13:56.630
Then they went up to Mike's bedroom.

00:13:56.690 --> 00:14:00.653
Mike closed the door and Kate put on some music.

00:14:00.713 --> 00:14:02.674
What do you think of the news?

00:14:02.734 --> 00:14:03.705
Asked Mike.

00:14:03.765 --> 00:14:05.416
I can hardly believe it.

00:14:05.476 --> 00:14:06.484
Said Kate.

00:14:06.544 --> 00:14:09.862
Where did you put Captain Salamanca's old treasure map?

00:14:09.922 --> 00:14:15.455
It's in a safe place, Said Mike, looking at the big bookshelf on the wall.

00:14:15.515 --> 00:14:19.418
Now we can study the map and start looking for the treasure.

00:14:19.478 --> 00:14:23.590
Dad will be busy with his work, and Mom always helps him.

00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:25.050
We'll be free.

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:27.722
This is going to be a great summer!

00:14:27.782 --> 00:14:28.979
Said Kate.

00:14:29.039 --> 00:14:31.046
Wait until I tell Carlos.

00:14:31.106 --> 00:14:33.376
Said Mike, picking up his cell phone.

00:14:33.436 --> 00:14:34.196
Yeah.

00:14:34.256 --> 00:14:35.227
Said Kate.

00:14:35.287 --> 00:14:37.438
And he can help us understand the map.

00:14:37.498 --> 00:14:41.428
The words are written in Spanish.

00:14:41.488 --> 00:14:44.670
Sharks.

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:47.550
A shark is a kind of fish.

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:51.930
There are about 400 different kinds of sharks.

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:59.970
Sharks live in different parts of the world, in the warm seas of the south, and in the cold waters of the north.

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:04.902
Some live at the bottom of the sea, and others swim near the coast.

00:15:04.962 --> 00:15:10.794
Sharks swam in the sea before dinosaurs walked on the earth.

00:15:10.854 --> 00:15:17.878
A lot of sharks are gray and have long bodies, but some sharks have different shapes.

00:15:17.938 --> 00:15:22.820
For example, hammerhead sharks have big, flat heads.

00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:28.052
Angel sharks live on the bottom of the sea and have flat bodies.

00:15:28.112 --> 00:15:32.484
Most sharks are between 60 and 90 centimeters long.

00:15:32.544 --> 00:15:37.686
The biggest shark is the whale shark, and it is longer than a bus.

00:15:37.746 --> 00:15:43.232
The smallest is the pygmy shark, and it is about the size of a banana.

00:15:43.292 --> 00:15:48.378
Most sharks have a lot of very strong teeth that look like triangles.

00:15:48.438 --> 00:15:52.570
When a shark loses a tooth, another grows in its place.

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:57.206
Sharks usually hunt alone, but sometimes they hunt in groups.

00:15:57.266 --> 00:15:59.600
Sharks are very good hunters.

00:15:59.661 --> 00:16:05.152
They can feel the movements of other animals near to them, and they can see well.

00:16:05.212 --> 00:16:11.233
Sharks can hear sounds from far away, like the sound of a boat or a ship.

00:16:11.293 --> 00:16:14.884
Sharks also have an excellent sense of smell.

00:16:14.944 --> 00:16:24.510
Most people think all sharks are dangerous, but some of the biggest sharks eat only very small plants and animals in the sea called plankton.

00:16:24.570 --> 00:16:28.156
One of the most dangerous sharks is the Great White.

00:16:28.216 --> 00:16:35.617
It usually attacks and kills seals, dolphins, other sharks, and sometimes people.

00:16:35.677 --> 00:16:38.388
The Great White Shark.

00:16:38.448 --> 00:16:45.499
The Great White Shark is about six meters long and weighs about 2,000 kilograms.

00:16:45.559 --> 00:16:48.730
It can live from 30 to 100 years.

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:57.042
In Steven Spielberg's 1975 film, Jaws, the Great White Shark is a terrible man-eater.

00:16:57.102 --> 00:17:00.353
But Great White Sharks don't usually eat people.

00:17:00.413 --> 00:17:05.484
They often think a person in the sea is a seal and attack it by mistake.

00:17:05.544 --> 00:17:08.986
Sometimes Great White Sharks attack boats.

00:17:09.046 --> 00:17:15.928
They are always very hungry, and sometimes they even eat objects like tins and bottles.

00:17:15.988 --> 00:17:19.214
Sharks in danger.

00:17:19.274 --> 00:17:22.741
Today, sharks are in danger.

00:17:22.801 --> 00:17:28.492
People kill them for sport, food, and sometimes by mistake.

00:17:28.552 --> 00:17:34.373
Soup, made from shark fins, is a popular dish in some parts of the world.

00:17:34.433 --> 00:17:41.995
Sometimes, fishermen catch sharks and cut off their fins, then they throw the sharks back into the sea.

00:17:42.055 --> 00:17:46.466
Without their fins, sharks cannot swim, and they die.

00:17:46.526 --> 00:17:56.881
Every year, more than 100 million sharks are killed, and some kinds of sharks are in danger of extinction.

00:17:56.941 --> 00:18:00.292
Chapter 3.

00:18:00.352 --> 00:18:07.406
The Treasure Map Mike's science class had a great time at Muir Woods National Park.

00:18:07.466 --> 00:18:13.596
Miss Williamson, the science teacher, showed them some of the world's oldest and tallest trees.

00:18:13.656 --> 00:18:20.774
She was everyone's favorite teacher at Galileo High because her classes were always interesting and fun.

00:18:20.834 --> 00:18:26.645
She started the Galileo Science Club, and Mike and Carlos were both members.

00:18:26.705 --> 00:18:31.216
There were club meetings every Wednesday afternoon after school.

00:18:31.276 --> 00:18:38.705
When Mike and Carlos came back from your woods, they went to Carlos's house to talk about their summer trip.

00:18:38.765 --> 00:18:41.258
I'm really excited about this trip.

00:18:41.318 --> 00:18:42.612
Said Carlos.

00:18:42.673 --> 00:18:46.048
With the old pirate map, we can look for the treasure.

00:18:46.108 --> 00:18:48.385
And if we're lucky, we'll find it.

00:18:48.446 --> 00:18:49.396
Said Mike.

00:18:49.456 --> 00:18:50.687
It won't be easy.

00:18:50.747 --> 00:18:51.898
Said Carlos.

00:18:51.958 --> 00:18:57.452
Pirates were clever people, and their maps had secret messages that are difficult to understand.

00:18:57.512 --> 00:18:59.283
Do you have the map with you?

00:18:59.343 --> 00:19:02.486
No, I hit it on the bookshelf in my room.

00:19:02.546 --> 00:19:03.656
Said Mike.

00:19:03.716 --> 00:19:05.888
Only Kate knows where it is.

00:19:05.948 --> 00:19:07.730
Do your parents know about it?

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:09.080
Asked Carlos.

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:10.692
No, not yet.

00:19:10.752 --> 00:19:11.772
Said Mike.

00:19:11.832 --> 00:19:15.826
My mom always says, be careful, it's dangerous.

00:19:15.886 --> 00:19:20.310
They laughed, and Carlos said, My parents are the same.

00:19:20.370 --> 00:19:23.862
Everything that's fun is dangerous.

00:19:23.923 --> 00:19:25.594
But we'll be careful.

00:19:25.654 --> 00:19:26.755
Said Mike.

00:19:26.815 --> 00:19:30.408
Next time, let's meet at your house and we can look at the map.

00:19:30.468 --> 00:19:31.538
Said Carlos.

00:19:31.598 --> 00:19:32.730
Good idea.

00:19:32.790 --> 00:19:33.850
Said Mike.

00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:36.052
It's all written in Spanish.

00:19:36.112 --> 00:19:37.984
No problem for me.

00:19:38.044 --> 00:19:40.396
Said Carlos, laughing.

00:19:40.456 --> 00:19:46.481
Friday was the last day of school, and everyone talked about their exciting vacation plans.

00:19:46.541 --> 00:19:57.354
That evening, Mr. Sullivan told his family more about the trip, and Mike and Kate listened carefully.

00:19:57.414 --> 00:20:04.904
We'll probably stay five or six days.

00:20:04.964 --> 00:20:11.577
I have to work at Point Reyes National Seashore and the Farallon Islands, and Mom is going to help me.

00:20:11.637 --> 00:20:14.568
Now, will you three be okay?

00:20:14.628 --> 00:20:17.490
Do you have something to do or will you get bored?

00:20:17.550 --> 00:20:19.770
Oh, we won't get bored, Dad.

00:20:19.830 --> 00:20:22.672
Said Kate, thinking about the treasure map.

00:20:22.732 --> 00:20:24.002
Don't worry, Dad.

00:20:24.062 --> 00:20:25.103
Said Mike.

00:20:25.163 --> 00:20:30.814
Kate Carlos and I can stay on the beach, play in the sea or go for walks in the hills.

00:20:30.875 --> 00:20:33.576
All right, said Mrs. Sullivan.

00:20:33.636 --> 00:20:37.269
You can stay on the beach, but you mustn't swim in the sea.

00:20:37.329 --> 00:20:42.974
Remember, this is the Pacific Ocean, and there are a lot of sharks, and they swim close to the beach.

00:20:43.034 --> 00:20:44.755
They're very dangerous.

00:20:44.815 --> 00:20:51.460
Mike laughed and said, we'll be careful, Mom, and we won't go swimming.

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:56.000
You're free to do what you want during the day, said Mr. Sullivan.

00:20:56.060 --> 00:21:00.186
But we'll meet for dinner on the Pelican every evening at about six.

00:21:00.246 --> 00:21:05.778
If you have any problems, just call or text Mom or me on our cell phones.

00:21:05.838 --> 00:21:09.870
Kate and Mike went upstairs and found Carlos.

00:21:09.930 --> 00:21:11.240
Hi, Carlos.

00:21:11.300 --> 00:21:12.261
Said Mike.

00:21:12.321 --> 00:21:14.522
Can you come to my house right now?

00:21:14.582 --> 00:21:17.423
We can look at the map and start making plans.

00:21:17.483 --> 00:21:19.254
I'll be there in ten minutes.

00:21:19.314 --> 00:21:21.364
Said Carlos happily.

00:21:21.424 --> 00:21:26.481
Mike took the old treasure map from the bookshelf and put it on his desk.

00:21:26.541 --> 00:21:31.660
When Carlos arrived, the three of them sat around the desk and looked at it carefully.

00:21:31.721 --> 00:21:34.532
Gee, this is exciting.

00:21:34.592 --> 00:21:36.483
Said Carlos, touching it.

00:21:36.543 --> 00:21:38.564
An old pirate map.

00:21:38.625 --> 00:21:43.637
Look, that's where Bodega Bay is, but it doesn't say that.

00:21:43.697 --> 00:21:45.838
It just says Bahia.

00:21:45.898 --> 00:21:53.655
That's interesting because today in Spanish, Bay is Bahia, but maybe the spelling was different in the 1600s.

00:21:53.715 --> 00:21:59.061
Looking at this map, we can see a town already existed there at that time.

00:21:59.121 --> 00:22:01.702
It was probably a pirate's town.

00:22:01.762 --> 00:22:02.883
Said Mike.

00:22:02.943 --> 00:22:07.266
There's a big harbor, the perfect place for pirates to hide.

00:22:07.326 --> 00:22:18.492
This is also very interesting because my book on the history of California says that Bodega Bay wasn't discovered until 1775.

00:22:18.552 --> 00:22:23.148
Looking at this map, people lived in the area long before.

00:22:23.208 --> 00:22:25.114
Look on the corner of the map.

00:22:25.174 --> 00:22:26.114
Said Kate.

00:22:26.174 --> 00:22:28.226
There's a date.

00:22:28.286 --> 00:22:28.966
1608.

00:22:29.026 --> 00:22:31.889
That's the year of the shipwreck of the Sonora.

00:22:31.949 --> 00:22:33.140
Said Carlos.

00:22:33.200 --> 00:22:39.696
Captain Salamanca probably hit his treasure that year before the shipwreck in November.

00:22:39.756 --> 00:22:42.758
What else does it say on his map?

00:22:42.818 --> 00:22:44.380
Asked Mike.

00:22:44.440 --> 00:22:49.343
Hmm, north of the town, there's the word Cementario.

00:22:49.403 --> 00:22:51.415
In Spanish, that means cemetery.

00:22:51.475 --> 00:22:52.666
Said Carlos.

00:22:52.726 --> 00:22:55.258
It was probably the town cemetery.

00:22:55.318 --> 00:23:01.042
Near the cemetery, there's a place called Hacienda Estrada.

00:23:01.102 --> 00:23:02.253
Said Mike.

00:23:02.313 --> 00:23:06.766
And there's a small river near it called Rio Estrada.

00:23:06.826 --> 00:23:09.978
Hacienda means a big farm or ranch.

00:23:10.038 --> 00:23:13.131
And Estrada was probably the name of the family who owned it.

00:23:13.191 --> 00:23:14.474
Said Carlos.

00:23:14.534 --> 00:23:18.269
Look, there's a drawing of a lighthouse on the coast.

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:19.320
Said Mike.

00:23:19.380 --> 00:23:23.693
There's a big black X east of the town with the word agua.

00:23:23.753 --> 00:23:24.764
Said Kate.

00:23:24.824 --> 00:23:26.795
Agua in Spanish means water.

00:23:26.855 --> 00:23:28.096
Said Carlos.

00:23:28.156 --> 00:23:31.358
That was probably where the pirates got their drinking water.

00:23:31.418 --> 00:23:32.900
A water well.

00:23:32.960 --> 00:23:38.823
There's some red lines that go south from the town to what is now Doran Beach.

00:23:38.883 --> 00:23:40.081
Said Mike.

00:23:40.141 --> 00:23:42.079
But where's the treasure?

00:23:42.139 --> 00:23:43.640
Asked Kate.

00:23:43.700 --> 00:23:45.181
Good question.

00:23:45.241 --> 00:23:46.192
Said Mike.

00:23:46.252 --> 00:23:49.774
The places on the map are probably important clues.

00:23:49.834 --> 00:23:52.216
We have almost a week to explore them.

00:23:52.276 --> 00:23:53.597
Said Carlos.

00:23:53.657 --> 00:23:55.898
Why don't we start with the water well?

00:23:55.958 --> 00:23:57.480
Said Kate excitedly.

00:23:57.540 --> 00:23:59.231
That's a good place to hide a treasure.

00:23:59.251 --> 00:24:00.562
Okay.

00:24:00.622 --> 00:24:02.192
Said Mike and Carlos.

00:24:02.252 --> 00:24:04.594
That'll be the first place we look.

00:24:04.654 --> 00:24:07.748
Said Mike.

00:24:07.808 --> 00:24:11.072
Chapter 4.

00:24:11.132 --> 00:24:19.285
The Treasure Chest The Pelican left Marina Harbor in San Francisco on a foggy Wednesday morning.

00:24:19.345 --> 00:24:27.327
Early in the afternoon, the Sullivan's and Carlos got to the town of Bodega Bay and moored the boat at the small pier.

00:24:27.387 --> 00:24:34.920
They had lunch, and then Mr. Sullivan said, Your mom and I have to start working and we're sailing to Point Reyes.

00:24:34.980 --> 00:24:37.134
We'll be back at the pier at dinner time.

00:24:37.194 --> 00:24:38.156
Have fun!

00:24:38.216 --> 00:24:39.408
Thanks!

00:24:39.468 --> 00:24:40.940
Said the three friends.

00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:42.501
See you at dinner!

00:24:42.562 --> 00:24:46.091
They got off the pelican and watched it sail away.

00:24:46.151 --> 00:24:47.411
Do you have the map?

00:24:47.471 --> 00:24:48.612
asked Carlos.

00:24:48.672 --> 00:24:50.632
Yeah, it's in my back.

00:24:50.692 --> 00:24:52.733
Said Mike, looking at his watch.

00:24:52.793 --> 00:24:54.504
It's half past two.

00:24:54.564 --> 00:24:57.445
We have about four hours before dinner time.

00:24:57.505 --> 00:24:58.975
This is exciting.

00:24:59.035 --> 00:24:59.936
Said Kate.

00:24:59.996 --> 00:25:02.336
We can start on our treasure hunt.

00:25:02.396 --> 00:25:08.064
Mike took the map out and said, let's start with the water well.

00:25:08.124 --> 00:25:11.251
The three friends looked at the map carefully.

00:25:11.311 --> 00:25:15.282
The water well is east of the town, said Carlos.

00:25:15.342 --> 00:25:18.752
The harbor is west of the town and the hills are east.

00:25:18.812 --> 00:25:20.773
We have to go to the hills.

00:25:20.833 --> 00:25:24.354
They looked east and saw some brown hills.

00:25:24.414 --> 00:25:29.355
Let's explore them, said Mike, and see if the water well is still there.

00:25:29.415 --> 00:25:31.766
We can follow this path.

00:25:31.826 --> 00:25:37.332
They followed the path into the hills and spent the afternoon looking for the water well.

00:25:37.393 --> 00:25:39.218
But they found nothing.

00:25:39.279 --> 00:25:44.791
Lucky had a lot of fun running up and down the hills, and everyone enjoyed watching him.

00:25:44.852 --> 00:25:48.283
I don't think there's a water well in these hills.

00:25:48.343 --> 00:25:51.144
Said Kate, who was hot and tired.

00:25:51.204 --> 00:25:52.975
And I'm thirsty.

00:25:53.035 --> 00:25:55.146
There's nothing in these hills.

00:25:55.206 --> 00:25:57.076
Said Carlos, laughing.

00:25:57.136 --> 00:25:59.836
Hey guys, it's almost five o'clock.

00:25:59.896 --> 00:26:00.726
Said Mike.

00:26:00.786 --> 00:26:02.247
It's time to go back.

00:26:02.307 --> 00:26:04.728
Dinner is at half past six.

00:26:04.788 --> 00:26:08.990
On the way back, we can stop at the supermarket and buy some cold drinks.

00:26:09.050 --> 00:26:10.230
Good idea.

00:26:10.290 --> 00:26:11.291
Said Kate.

00:26:11.351 --> 00:26:13.322
We didn't have much luck today.

00:26:13.382 --> 00:26:17.372
We'll explore the area south of Bodega Bay tomorrow.

00:26:17.432 --> 00:26:18.593
Said Mike.

00:26:18.653 --> 00:26:22.786
Yeah, there are red lines that go all the way to Doran Beach.

00:26:22.846 --> 00:26:24.117
Said Carlos.

00:26:24.177 --> 00:26:26.589
Red lines probably mean something.

00:26:26.649 --> 00:26:27.830
I hope so.

00:26:27.890 --> 00:26:29.541
Said Mike.

00:26:29.601 --> 00:26:37.086
Dinner time was fun because Mrs. Sullivan cooked a great meal and everyone had something to say about the day.

00:26:37.146 --> 00:26:41.280
After dinner, they all played cards and went to bed early.

00:26:41.340 --> 00:26:46.435
The next morning, Mrs. Sullivan made sandwiches for Kate, Mike, and Carlos.

00:26:46.496 --> 00:26:49.998
Dad and I are going to go to Point Reyes again today.

00:26:50.058 --> 00:26:51.359
Said Mrs. Sullivan.

00:26:51.419 --> 00:26:52.809
Where are you going?

00:26:52.870 --> 00:26:56.201
Oh, we're going to take a long walk on the beach.

00:26:56.261 --> 00:26:57.492
Said Kate.

00:26:57.552 --> 00:27:00.703
Don't forget to put on some sun protection then.

00:27:00.763 --> 00:27:02.054
See you at dinner.

00:27:02.114 --> 00:27:03.404
Said Mrs. Sullivan.

00:27:03.464 --> 00:27:04.875
Have fun!

00:27:04.935 --> 00:27:11.480
Kate, Mike, and Carlos started walking south to Doran Beach, and Lucky ran ahead of them.

00:27:11.540 --> 00:27:17.185
It was a beautiful sunny day, and there were a lot of people on the beach enjoying the sun.

00:27:17.245 --> 00:27:21.036
Behind the Long Beach, there was a tall cliff.

00:27:21.096 --> 00:27:25.078
Suddenly, Carlos saw a small opening in the cliff.

00:27:25.138 --> 00:27:27.149
Hey, look over there.

00:27:27.209 --> 00:27:29.870
He said, there's a small opening.

00:27:29.930 --> 00:27:32.451
Let's go inside and look around.

00:27:32.511 --> 00:27:33.842
Said Mike.

00:27:33.902 --> 00:27:37.294
Kate, Carlos and Lucky slowly followed him.

00:27:37.354 --> 00:27:39.244
It's a cave.

00:27:39.304 --> 00:27:41.214
Said Carlos excitedly.

00:27:41.274 --> 00:27:43.004
Did you bring a flashlight?

00:27:43.064 --> 00:27:44.695
Yeah, here it is.

00:27:44.755 --> 00:27:46.895
Said Mike, turning it on.

00:27:46.955 --> 00:27:50.596
Look, there's some stone steps that go down.

00:27:50.656 --> 00:27:52.756
Perhaps they go to another cave.

00:27:52.816 --> 00:27:54.776
Said Carlos, let's go.

00:27:54.836 --> 00:27:57.407
Is this where the treasure is, do you think?

00:27:57.467 --> 00:27:58.647
Asked Kate.

00:27:58.707 --> 00:28:00.408
It's a good hiding place.

00:28:00.468 --> 00:28:03.928
Said Mike, walking slowly down the stone steps.

00:28:03.988 --> 00:28:07.439
Gee, it's really dark and scary in here.

00:28:07.499 --> 00:28:08.931
Said Kate.

00:28:08.991 --> 00:28:14.697
The three friends walked into another cave, and there was some seawater on the ground.

00:28:14.757 --> 00:28:17.019
It's not very dark in here.

00:28:17.079 --> 00:28:18.770
Said Mike, looking up.

00:28:18.830 --> 00:28:21.642
There's a hole up there, a small opening.

00:28:21.702 --> 00:28:22.703
Said Carlos.

00:28:22.764 --> 00:28:24.525
And I can see the sky.

00:28:24.585 --> 00:28:26.506
How strange.

00:28:26.567 --> 00:28:29.659
Said Kate, who was a bit nervous.

00:28:29.719 --> 00:28:33.279
They looked around the cave, but it was empty.

00:28:33.340 --> 00:28:35.909
Then suddenly Carlos saw something.

00:28:35.969 --> 00:28:38.160
Mike, come here with your flashlight.

00:28:38.220 --> 00:28:39.280
Cried Carlos.

00:28:39.340 --> 00:28:42.211
There's something in the corner over here.

00:28:42.271 --> 00:28:43.742
Ah, let's see.

00:28:43.802 --> 00:28:47.393
Said Mike, looking in the dark corner with his flashlight.

00:28:47.453 --> 00:28:50.754
There's a big old box.

00:28:50.814 --> 00:28:51.755
Box?

00:28:51.815 --> 00:28:52.885
Cried Kate.

00:28:52.945 --> 00:28:54.876
It's the treasure chest.

00:28:54.936 --> 00:29:01.062
The three friends were surprised and looked at each other and Lucky started barking.

00:29:01.122 --> 00:29:03.286
You're right!"

00:29:03.346 --> 00:29:05.128
cried Mike and Carlos.

00:29:05.188 --> 00:29:07.379
They looked at the big wooden box.

00:29:07.439 --> 00:29:08.990
It was very old.

00:29:09.050 --> 00:29:10.391
It's the treasure!

00:29:10.451 --> 00:29:12.022
said Kate excitedly.

00:29:12.082 --> 00:29:14.814
But we don't know what's inside.

00:29:14.874 --> 00:29:16.155
Said Carlos.

00:29:16.215 --> 00:29:18.146
Well, let's open it.

00:29:18.206 --> 00:29:19.037
Said Mike.

00:29:19.097 --> 00:29:20.738
There's a big lock on it.

00:29:20.798 --> 00:29:21.729
Said Kate.

00:29:21.789 --> 00:29:23.900
Let's break the old lock.

00:29:23.960 --> 00:29:25.221
Said Mike.

00:29:25.281 --> 00:29:29.194
Mike took a big stone and hit the lock a few times.

00:29:29.254 --> 00:29:30.758
But it didn't break.

00:29:30.818 --> 00:29:32.604
Here, said Kate.

00:29:32.664 --> 00:29:33.934
Try with this stone.

00:29:33.994 --> 00:29:35.616
It's much bigger.

00:29:35.676 --> 00:29:38.278
But the old lock didn't break.

00:29:38.338 --> 00:29:42.292
Let me try, said Carlos, hitting the lock again.

00:29:42.352 --> 00:29:51.208
Suddenly, the old lock broke, and they were ready to open Captain Salamanca's treasure chest.

00:29:51.269 --> 00:29:54.672
Chapter 5.

00:29:54.732 --> 00:29:57.066
Well done, Lucky.

00:29:57.126 --> 00:30:00.080
Who's going to open the treasure chest?"

00:30:00.140 --> 00:30:02.460
asked Carlos, looking at Mike and Kate.

00:30:02.520 --> 00:30:04.931
Mike, you took the old map.

00:30:04.991 --> 00:30:06.042
Said Kate.

00:30:06.102 --> 00:30:09.122
So, you can open the treasure chest.

00:30:09.183 --> 00:30:12.514
Mike slowly opened the old chest.

00:30:12.574 --> 00:30:17.304
Suddenly, the three friends jumped back and Kate screamed.

00:30:17.365 --> 00:30:20.176
There was something terrible inside.

00:30:20.236 --> 00:30:21.536
A skeleton.

00:30:21.596 --> 00:30:24.752
Lucky started barking loudly.

00:30:24.812 --> 00:30:30.310
The skeleton was wearing pirates' clothes and a big black hat.

00:30:30.370 --> 00:30:35.124
Mike, Kate, and Carlos stared at it and didn't know what to say.

00:30:35.184 --> 00:30:38.046
They were very surprised and scared.

00:30:38.106 --> 00:30:40.007
Kate spoke first.

00:30:40.067 --> 00:30:42.068
Is this the treasure?

00:30:42.128 --> 00:30:43.750
It's terrible!

00:30:43.810 --> 00:30:47.772
Maybe there's something else in the treasure chest, said Carlos.

00:30:47.832 --> 00:30:51.784
He slowly moved closer to the chest and looked inside.

00:30:51.844 --> 00:30:56.845
There's nothing inside except the skeleton," he said sadly.

00:30:56.905 --> 00:31:02.838
Why did someone put the body of a pirate inside the treasure chest and lock it?

00:31:02.898 --> 00:31:04.598
asked Mike.

00:31:04.658 --> 00:31:08.620
Suddenly, Lucky started barking again.

00:31:08.681 --> 00:31:14.283
The three friends turned around and saw that water was coming down the stone steps.

00:31:14.343 --> 00:31:15.744
What's happening?

00:31:15.804 --> 00:31:17.475
asked Kate nervously.

00:31:17.535 --> 00:31:20.031
Why is water coming in here?

00:31:20.092 --> 00:31:22.488
Oh no, the tide!

00:31:22.548 --> 00:31:23.539
Said Mike.

00:31:23.599 --> 00:31:27.762
It's high tide, and these caves fill up with seawater.

00:31:27.822 --> 00:31:29.813
We have to get out of here now.

00:31:29.873 --> 00:31:31.644
But wait, said Carlos.

00:31:31.704 --> 00:31:35.836
Perhaps there's a clue or another map in the skeleton's clothes in his pockets.

00:31:35.896 --> 00:31:38.598
Are you going to touch it?

00:31:38.658 --> 00:31:40.760
Asked Kate, who was scared.

00:31:40.820 --> 00:31:42.911
I'll just touch his clothes.

00:31:42.971 --> 00:31:44.052
Said Carlos.

00:31:44.112 --> 00:31:45.262
We have to hurry.

00:31:45.322 --> 00:31:46.103
Said Mike.

00:31:46.163 --> 00:31:50.078
If more water comes in, we'll be in big trouble.

00:31:50.138 --> 00:31:53.504
Carlos started touching the skeleton's clothes.

00:31:53.564 --> 00:31:56.785
He looked in all the pockets but found nothing.

00:31:56.845 --> 00:32:00.827
Then he took off the big black hat and looked inside it.

00:32:00.887 --> 00:32:03.078
There's something inside the hat!

00:32:03.138 --> 00:32:04.278
cried Carlos.

00:32:04.338 --> 00:32:09.972
It's an old piece of paper that says Juan Martinez de los Robles.

00:32:10.032 --> 00:32:13.780
He took the old piece of paper and showed it to Kate and Mike.

00:32:13.840 --> 00:32:15.658
Maybe that was his name.

00:32:15.718 --> 00:32:16.819
Said Kate.

00:32:16.879 --> 00:32:19.060
No, I don't think so.

00:32:19.120 --> 00:32:20.061
Said Mike.

00:32:20.121 --> 00:32:24.744
You don't write your name on a piece of paper and put it in your hat.

00:32:24.804 --> 00:32:27.406
I think it's a clue.

00:32:27.466 --> 00:32:30.978
Carlos quickly put the piece of paper in his pocket.

00:32:31.038 --> 00:32:34.134
Lucky started barking loudly again.

00:32:34.194 --> 00:32:37.810
because a lot of water was now coming into the cave.

00:32:37.870 --> 00:32:39.542
Mike picked him up.

00:32:39.602 --> 00:32:47.550
The three friends couldn't get out because water was coming down the stone steps, and the cave was quickly filling up with water.

00:32:47.610 --> 00:32:49.592
They were in big trouble.

00:32:49.653 --> 00:32:51.394
How can we get out of here?

00:32:51.454 --> 00:32:54.498
asked Kate, who was now starting to get very scared.

00:32:54.558 --> 00:32:56.762
The water is almost up to my knees.

00:32:56.822 --> 00:33:02.627
There's only one way out," said Mike, looking at the small hole high above their heads.

00:33:02.687 --> 00:33:04.678
But we can't climb up there.

00:33:04.738 --> 00:33:05.778
Said Carlos.

00:33:05.838 --> 00:33:07.128
It's impossible.

00:33:07.188 --> 00:33:10.390
We need someone on the outside to throw down a rope.

00:33:10.450 --> 00:33:12.980
I have an idea, said Mike.

00:33:13.040 --> 00:33:17.662
Kate, if you hold Lucky, Carlos and I can lift you.

00:33:17.722 --> 00:33:20.983
Then you can push Lucky up to the top.

00:33:21.043 --> 00:33:24.778
He is small and light and can get out of the hole.

00:33:24.838 --> 00:33:33.055
Mike looked at Lucky, who was in his arms, and said, Listen carefully Lucky, go and find help!

00:33:33.115 --> 00:33:36.446
Carlos and Mike lifted Kate and Lucky.

00:33:36.506 --> 00:33:42.559
It wasn't easy, but they were able to get Kate quite high, and she pushed Lucky outside.

00:33:42.619 --> 00:33:51.672
There were a lot of people on the beach that day, and when Lucky got out of the hole, he started barking loudly and running around.

00:33:51.732 --> 00:33:54.632
What's that dog doing?

00:33:54.692 --> 00:33:58.423
Said a tall young man who was sitting on the beach with some friends.

00:33:58.483 --> 00:34:00.114
He's very excited.

00:34:00.174 --> 00:34:01.224
Said his friend.

00:34:01.284 --> 00:34:03.085
He's trying to tell us something.

00:34:03.145 --> 00:34:05.066
Perhaps someone needs help.

00:34:05.126 --> 00:34:06.576
Said another young man.

00:34:06.636 --> 00:34:08.717
Let's follow him and see.

00:34:08.777 --> 00:34:13.348
The four young men followed Lucky to the small hole and looked inside.

00:34:13.408 --> 00:34:15.139
Does anyone need help?

00:34:15.199 --> 00:34:17.153
Shouted the tall young man.

00:34:17.213 --> 00:34:22.377
Yes, the water in the cave is up to our knees and we can't get out.

00:34:22.437 --> 00:34:23.638
Shouted Mike.

00:34:23.698 --> 00:34:25.758
Can you please help us?

00:34:25.818 --> 00:34:27.479
It's high tide.

00:34:27.539 --> 00:34:29.109
Shouted the young man.

00:34:29.169 --> 00:34:32.020
Don't worry, we can get you out of there.

00:34:32.080 --> 00:34:34.251
I've got a rope in my car.

00:34:34.311 --> 00:34:36.641
Wait a moment and I'll be back.

00:34:36.702 --> 00:34:42.490
He ran across the beach to the parking lot, got a long rope from his car and ran back.

00:34:42.550 --> 00:34:44.519
Okay, listen.

00:34:44.578 --> 00:34:47.489
Shouted the young man who was standing over the hole.

00:34:47.549 --> 00:34:50.110
I'm gonna send this rope down to you.

00:34:50.170 --> 00:34:51.620
Hold on to it.

00:34:51.680 --> 00:34:54.731
Then my friends and I will pull you up.

00:34:54.791 --> 00:34:56.332
Okay.

00:34:56.392 --> 00:34:58.932
Shouted Kate, Mike, and Carlos.

00:34:58.992 --> 00:35:04.394
The four young men pulled Kate up first, then Carlos, and then Mike.

00:35:04.454 --> 00:35:07.525
Lucky jumped into Kate's arms and looked at her.

00:35:07.585 --> 00:35:08.885
Thanks, Lucky.

00:35:08.945 --> 00:35:12.055
Said Kate, smiling at the little black dog.

00:35:12.115 --> 00:35:13.744
And thank you.

00:35:13.804 --> 00:35:16.315
She said, looking at the four young men.

00:35:16.376 --> 00:35:17.256
Yeah.

00:35:17.316 --> 00:35:18.076
Said Mike.

00:35:18.136 --> 00:35:19.346
Thanks a lot.

00:35:19.406 --> 00:35:21.247
You were very kind to help us.

00:35:21.307 --> 00:35:22.318
Said Carlos.

00:35:22.378 --> 00:35:24.888
We were in big trouble down there.

00:35:24.948 --> 00:35:26.870
You guys are lucky.

00:35:26.930 --> 00:35:27.900
Said one of the men.

00:35:27.920 --> 00:35:32.641
I always keep a rope in my car because my friends and I are mountain climbers.

00:35:32.702 --> 00:35:34.752
What were you doing in the cave?

00:35:34.812 --> 00:35:36.518
Ask the tall young man.

00:35:36.578 --> 00:35:39.585
Oh, we were just looking around?

00:35:39.645 --> 00:35:42.095
Said Mike, and his face became red.

00:35:42.115 --> 00:35:44.016
Oh well, it's getting late.

00:35:44.076 --> 00:35:44.976
Said Kate.

00:35:45.036 --> 00:35:47.206
We have to go back to Bodega Bay.

00:35:47.266 --> 00:35:49.027
Thanks again for your help.

00:35:49.087 --> 00:35:50.697
We were happy to help you.

00:35:50.757 --> 00:35:52.217
Said the tall young man.

00:35:52.277 --> 00:35:54.948
But next time, be careful.

00:35:55.008 --> 00:35:57.118
Okay, we will.

00:35:57.178 --> 00:36:00.679
Said the three friends.

00:36:00.740 --> 00:36:03.980
Pirates.

00:36:04.040 --> 00:36:09.495
A long time ago, ships were the only form of transport to cross the sea.

00:36:09.555 --> 00:36:12.948
The seas were full of pirates and they robbed ships.

00:36:13.009 --> 00:36:16.012
Sometimes they killed the crew too.

00:36:16.072 --> 00:36:18.764
Pirates were dangerous people.

00:36:18.824 --> 00:36:22.668
Their sailing ships usually had the Jolly Roger flag.

00:36:22.728 --> 00:36:26.232
Let's take a look at some pirates from the past.

00:36:26.292 --> 00:36:28.050
Blackbeard.

00:36:28.110 --> 00:36:34.944
The most famous pirate was probably Edward Teach, 1680-1718.

00:36:35.004 --> 00:36:39.468
He was called Blackbeard because he had a long Blackbeard.

00:36:39.529 --> 00:36:44.794
He always wore a lot of knives and guns because he wanted to scare people.

00:36:44.854 --> 00:36:50.969
He and his pirates robbed a lot of ships in the Caribbean Sea and in the Atlantic Ocean.

00:36:51.029 --> 00:36:56.440
Blackbeard had a very big treasure, but no one knows where he hid it.

00:36:56.500 --> 00:37:00.601
He was killed during a long battle with the British Navy.

00:37:00.662 --> 00:37:02.662
Black Bart.

00:37:02.722 --> 00:37:10.336
Bartholomew Roberts, 1682-1722, was another famous pirate.

00:37:10.396 --> 00:37:15.946
He was also called Black Bart, and he was a very successful pirate.

00:37:16.006 --> 00:37:26.591
Between 1719 and 1722, he robbed more than 470 ships in the Caribbean Sea and in the Atlantic Ocean.

00:37:26.651 --> 00:37:31.604
He was an unusual pirate because he was always clean and well-dressed.

00:37:31.664 --> 00:37:34.716
He liked reading books and listening to music.

00:37:34.776 --> 00:37:37.458
There were always musicians on his ships.

00:37:37.518 --> 00:37:40.670
He was killed during a battle at sea.

00:37:40.730 --> 00:37:45.093
Anne Bonny, Mary Reed, and Calico Jack.

00:37:45.153 --> 00:37:55.098
Anne Bonnie, 1700-1782, was Irish, and Mary Reed, 1690-1721, was English.

00:37:55.158 --> 00:37:57.008
They were female pirates.

00:37:57.069 --> 00:38:02.660
In the early 1700s, they dressed like men and fought like men.

00:38:02.720 --> 00:38:08.312
Anne Bonnie loved another pirate, Calico Jack, 1682-1720.

00:38:08.372 --> 00:38:15.054
Anne, Mary and Calico Jack lived together as pirates in the Caribbean Sea.

00:38:15.114 --> 00:38:19.388
Together they robbed a lot of ships and had a big treasure.

00:38:19.448 --> 00:38:27.063
In 1720, after a battle with a British ship, Anne, Mary and Calico Jack were put in prison.

00:38:27.123 --> 00:38:31.105
Calico Jack was hanged and Mary died in prison.

00:38:31.166 --> 00:38:36.780
People think that Anne left prison and went to live in the American colonies.

00:38:36.840 --> 00:38:38.979
Pirates today.

00:38:39.039 --> 00:38:42.909
Today there are modern pirates in different parts of the world.

00:38:42.969 --> 00:38:50.253
Indonesia, the Philippines, the South China Sea, Somalia, Brazil, and the Florida coast.

00:38:50.313 --> 00:38:55.346
They are dangerous and have fast modern boats and big guns.

00:38:55.406 --> 00:38:57.997
They go on to ships and rob them.

00:38:58.057 --> 00:39:08.930
Military forces around the world and international organizations, such as the United Nations, have a difficult job trying to stop them.

00:39:08.990 --> 00:39:12.257
Chapter 6.

00:39:12.317 --> 00:39:14.928
The Hacienda Estrada.

00:39:14.988 --> 00:39:19.618
Mike, Kate, and Carlos got back to the Pelican at dinner time.

00:39:19.678 --> 00:39:22.259
Hi, said Mr. Sullivan.

00:39:22.319 --> 00:39:25.920
We did a lot of interesting work today at Point Reyes.

00:39:25.980 --> 00:39:29.940
We saw two great white shark swimming by.

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:32.811
Tomorrow we're going to the Farillon Islands.

00:39:32.871 --> 00:39:34.571
How was your day?

00:39:34.631 --> 00:39:36.432
Asked Mrs. Sullivan.

00:39:36.492 --> 00:39:38.418
Ah, interesting.

00:39:38.478 --> 00:39:41.194
said Mike, looking at his sister and Carlos.

00:39:41.254 --> 00:39:43.885
We explored the beach, said Carlos.

00:39:43.945 --> 00:39:46.225
Are you guys getting bored?

00:39:46.285 --> 00:39:47.636
asked Mr. Sullivan.

00:39:47.696 --> 00:39:48.716
Bored?

00:39:48.776 --> 00:39:50.357
said Kate, smiling.

00:39:50.417 --> 00:39:52.457
No, of course not.

00:39:52.517 --> 00:39:57.869
The next morning after breakfast, Mr. and Mrs. Sullivan sailed to the Farallon Islands.

00:39:57.929 --> 00:40:04.874
It was a foggy morning, and the three friends stood on the pier and talked about their scary adventure in the cave.

00:40:04.934 --> 00:40:10.629
Carlos took out the old piece of paper he found in the skeleton's hat and looked at it.

00:40:10.689 --> 00:40:12.489
Is this a clue?

00:40:12.550 --> 00:40:14.000
What does it mean?

00:40:14.060 --> 00:40:15.261
He asked.

00:40:15.321 --> 00:40:16.911
It's the name of a man.

00:40:16.931 --> 00:40:18.972
Or perhaps it isn't.

00:40:19.032 --> 00:40:20.242
Said Kate.

00:40:20.303 --> 00:40:22.694
Let's take another look at the map.

00:40:22.754 --> 00:40:23.754
Said Mike.

00:40:23.814 --> 00:40:28.226
Why don't we go to the tourist office and ask about the Hacienda Astrada?

00:40:28.286 --> 00:40:29.426
Said Kate.

00:40:29.486 --> 00:40:32.119
Perhaps we can get some useful information.

00:40:32.179 --> 00:40:34.242
Okay, said Carlos.

00:40:34.302 --> 00:40:37.384
I'm sure the treasure is here somewhere.

00:40:37.444 --> 00:40:44.818
Margaret Healy worked at the Bodega Bay tourist office and knew all about the history of the town.

00:40:44.878 --> 00:40:51.126
The Estrada family was a rich and important family in the 1600s, said Margaret.

00:40:51.187 --> 00:40:57.936
They were the first to build a home and a big farm here, the Hacienda Estrada.

00:40:57.996 --> 00:41:05.930
The family's only daughter was called Isabella and she married a sea captain called Juan Martinez.

00:41:05.990 --> 00:41:13.806
Soon after their marriage, he was killed during a terrible fight with pirates and his young wife never married again.

00:41:13.866 --> 00:41:17.128
She was always sad and dressed in black.

00:41:17.188 --> 00:41:19.359
She rarely left the Hacienda.

00:41:19.419 --> 00:41:21.188
What a sad story.

00:41:21.248 --> 00:41:22.676
Said Kate.

00:41:22.736 --> 00:41:28.582
Was the captain's last name Robles or Delos Robles?

00:41:28.643 --> 00:41:29.844
asked Mike.

00:41:29.904 --> 00:41:30.804
No.

00:41:30.864 --> 00:41:32.196
Answered Margaret.

00:41:32.256 --> 00:41:34.988
His last name was Martinez.

00:41:35.049 --> 00:41:36.620
Where was he buried?

00:41:36.680 --> 00:41:38.031
asked Carlos.

00:41:38.092 --> 00:41:39.473
No one knows.

00:41:39.533 --> 00:41:40.704
Said Margaret.

00:41:40.764 --> 00:41:43.227
What about the old town cemetery?

00:41:43.287 --> 00:41:44.432
asked Kate.

00:41:44.493 --> 00:41:50.638
It's about 400 years old, and no one can read the names on the tombstones anymore.

00:41:50.698 --> 00:41:51.748
She said.

00:41:51.808 --> 00:41:58.110
If you're looking for old Spanish things, go and see the lighthouse at Twin Oaks Point.

00:41:58.170 --> 00:42:00.050
It's on the cliff.

00:42:00.110 --> 00:42:03.171
The three friends thanked her and left.

00:42:03.231 --> 00:42:08.992
They decided to follow the treasure map and go to the area northwest of Bodega Bay.

00:42:09.052 --> 00:42:13.356
They climbed up the Green Hills and stopped near a stone wall.

00:42:13.416 --> 00:42:14.829
What's this?"

00:42:14.889 --> 00:42:16.910
asked Mike, looking at the map.

00:42:16.970 --> 00:42:21.254
It looks like part of the old Hacienda Estrada, said Carlos.

00:42:21.314 --> 00:42:23.965
Look, there's a small river nearby, too.

00:42:24.025 --> 00:42:26.537
The same river that's on the map.

00:42:26.597 --> 00:42:30.920
They looked around and saw another stone wall and some steps.

00:42:30.980 --> 00:42:33.692
This looks like a wall of a house.

00:42:33.752 --> 00:42:35.363
Maybe the Hacienda.

00:42:35.423 --> 00:42:36.574
Said Kate.

00:42:36.634 --> 00:42:39.576
Yeah, but there's almost nothing here.

00:42:39.636 --> 00:42:40.790
Said Mike.

00:42:40.850 --> 00:42:44.884
Let's move on and see if we can find the cemetery.

00:42:44.944 --> 00:42:48.735
They walked to the cliff and a strong wind was blowing.

00:42:48.795 --> 00:42:51.826
From the top of the cliff they could see the Pacific Ocean.

00:42:51.886 --> 00:42:53.756
What a beautiful place.

00:42:53.816 --> 00:42:56.517
Said Kate, looking at the green blue sea.

00:42:56.577 --> 00:42:58.497
Let's stop here and have lunch.

00:42:58.557 --> 00:42:59.797
I'm hungry.

00:42:59.857 --> 00:43:01.118
We are too.

00:43:01.178 --> 00:43:02.918
Said Mike and Carlos.

00:43:02.978 --> 00:43:07.060
They sat down and had chicken sandwiches and fruit juice.

00:43:07.120 --> 00:43:10.024
Hey, look down there!"

00:43:10.084 --> 00:43:12.536
said Carlo, seeding his sandwich.

00:43:12.596 --> 00:43:20.417
From the top of the cliff, they saw the old cemetery that was on Salamanca's map and the old Spanish lighthouse.

00:43:20.477 --> 00:43:25.456
After lunch, they slowly climbed down and got to the old cemetery.

00:43:25.516 --> 00:43:28.312
There isn't much here, said Mike.

00:43:28.372 --> 00:43:32.614
Just a few very old tombstones and lots of grass.

00:43:32.674 --> 00:43:34.876
Gee, look at this one.

00:43:34.936 --> 00:43:35.936
Said Kate.

00:43:35.996 --> 00:43:40.840
I can't read the name, but the date is 1624.

00:43:40.900 --> 00:43:43.341
This place is probably full of ghosts.

00:43:43.401 --> 00:43:43.972
Let's go.

00:43:43.992 --> 00:43:45.432
I'm scared.

00:43:45.493 --> 00:43:50.546
Carlos laughed and said, We'll never find the treasure here.

00:43:50.606 --> 00:43:52.617
Perhaps there isn't any treasure.

00:43:52.677 --> 00:43:53.678
Said Kate.

00:43:53.738 --> 00:43:55.649
I'm sure there's a treasure.

00:43:55.709 --> 00:43:56.520
Said Mike.

00:43:56.580 --> 00:44:00.332
Don't forget that Captain Salamanca was looking for it.

00:44:00.392 --> 00:44:02.043
And we have his map.

00:44:02.103 --> 00:44:03.314
You're right, Mike.

00:44:03.374 --> 00:44:04.594
Said Carlos.

00:44:04.654 --> 00:44:07.286
We have to study the clues carefully.

00:44:07.346 --> 00:44:12.058
The name Juan Martinez de los Robles means something.

00:44:12.118 --> 00:44:13.890
But what?

00:44:13.950 --> 00:44:18.172
We have to find out.

00:44:18.232 --> 00:44:22.697
Listening activity.

00:44:22.757 --> 00:44:24.803
Good morning.

00:44:24.863 --> 00:44:26.404
How can I help you?

00:44:26.464 --> 00:44:27.951
A good morning.

00:44:28.011 --> 00:44:32.152
My friends and I are looking for Hacienda Estrada.

00:44:32.212 --> 00:44:34.333
What's the best way to get there?

00:44:34.393 --> 00:44:37.434
Well, there are two ways to get there.

00:44:37.494 --> 00:44:52.317
You can follow the small road on the right side of the supermarket parking lot and when you get to a big tree, turn right and keep walking until you see the old stone water well and turn left.

00:44:52.377 --> 00:44:54.297
It's the fastest road.

00:44:54.358 --> 00:44:56.938
How long will it take us to get there?

00:44:56.998 --> 00:45:02.180
Well, it'll take you about two hours if the weather is good.

00:45:02.240 --> 00:45:08.052
But remember to wear good climbing shoes because the road is in bad condition.

00:45:08.112 --> 00:45:09.562
It's dangerous.

00:45:09.622 --> 00:45:12.163
And remember to bring some water too.

00:45:12.223 --> 00:45:14.484
Climbing can make you thirsty.

00:45:14.544 --> 00:45:20.485
The last time I went there I had to bring a hat and an umbrella because it was raining.

00:45:20.545 --> 00:45:26.222
We want to go to Tomales Bay to see the show at the Tomales Bay Museum.

00:45:26.282 --> 00:45:28.158
How can we get there?

00:45:28.218 --> 00:45:32.020
There are three shows in Tomales Bay this summer.

00:45:32.080 --> 00:45:40.047
One is on sharks in the Pacific Ocean, the other is on pirate ships, and still another is on seabirds.

00:45:40.107 --> 00:45:42.148
Which one do you want to see?

00:45:42.208 --> 00:45:46.448
We're really interested in pirate ships and in sharks.

00:45:46.508 --> 00:45:56.080
The show on pirate ships opens at 10 in the morning and closes after lunch, and the one on sharks opens at 2 in the afternoon.

00:45:56.140 --> 00:46:01.743
If you catch the ferry boat today at half past 11, you can see the show on sharks.

00:46:01.803 --> 00:46:09.288
But if you want to see the one on pirate ships, then you have to catch the early morning ferry at half past 8.

00:46:09.348 --> 00:46:13.391
Where can we catch the ferry boat for Tomales Bay?

00:46:13.452 --> 00:46:22.600
On weekdays, the ferry boat leaves from pier number three at half past eight and from pier number five at half past eleven.

00:46:22.660 --> 00:46:26.192
You can buy tickets from the ferry boat office on the pier.

00:46:26.252 --> 00:46:36.676
On weekends though, all ferry boats for Tomales Bay leave from pier number one at the same times and you must buy tickets on the boat.

00:46:36.736 --> 00:46:40.436
How much of ferry boat tickets to Tomales Bay?

00:46:40.496 --> 00:46:47.302
On weekdays, round trip tickets cost $15 each, and on weekends they cost $18.

00:46:47.362 --> 00:46:50.063
Can we buy lunch on the ferry?

00:46:50.124 --> 00:46:51.434
Yes, you can.

00:46:51.494 --> 00:46:58.296
There's a special meal deal that costs eight dollars, and you get a big hamburger, fries, and a drink.

00:46:58.356 --> 00:47:02.167
Or you can spend only six dollars and get a smaller lunch.

00:47:02.227 --> 00:47:05.278
A cheese sandwich, an apple, and a drink.

00:47:05.338 --> 00:47:10.739
And if you add just one dollar to the price of the special ticket, you get a bag of cookies.

00:47:10.799 --> 00:47:12.620
Oh, that sounds great.

00:47:12.680 --> 00:47:15.628
Thank you.

00:47:15.688 --> 00:47:25.891
Chapter 7 The Old Lighthouse Let's go and see the old lighthouse at Twin Oaks Point, said Carlos.

00:47:25.952 --> 00:47:28.374
Lighthouses are always interesting.

00:47:28.434 --> 00:47:33.747
It was a windy day, and they walked along the cliff for almost an hour to get there.

00:47:33.807 --> 00:47:39.422
There was an old stone lighthouse on the cliff above the sea near two big oak trees.

00:47:39.482 --> 00:47:44.334
This was probably an important lighthouse in Captain Salamanca's days.

00:47:44.394 --> 00:47:45.425
Said Mike.

00:47:45.485 --> 00:47:48.877
Those two big oak trees look very old too.

00:47:48.937 --> 00:47:52.159
That's why people called it Twin Oaks Point.

00:47:52.219 --> 00:47:54.202
Said Kate laughing.

00:47:54.263 --> 00:47:58.346
Carlos suddenly turned around and looked at the two oak trees.

00:47:58.406 --> 00:48:00.968
Wait a minute, he said.

00:48:01.028 --> 00:48:09.981
The Spanish word for oak is robla, and the words de los roblas are written next to Juan Martinez's name.

00:48:10.041 --> 00:48:12.292
That means of the oaks.

00:48:12.352 --> 00:48:16.690
Perhaps roblas isn't part of his last name, but a clue.

00:48:16.750 --> 00:48:18.697
Oh, you're right, Carlos!"

00:48:18.758 --> 00:48:19.728
said Mike.

00:48:19.788 --> 00:48:22.368
Robles could be a clue.

00:48:22.428 --> 00:48:24.989
Perhaps he is buried under the oak trees.

00:48:25.049 --> 00:48:27.580
There are only two oaks in this area.

00:48:27.640 --> 00:48:30.631
Said Kate, looking at the two big trees.

00:48:30.691 --> 00:48:34.362
The three friends ran to the oak trees and looked around.

00:48:34.422 --> 00:48:37.132
There was a lot of tall grass under them.

00:48:37.192 --> 00:48:45.680
Suddenly Mike said, Look, under the grass there's a small tombstone and half of it is underground.

00:48:45.741 --> 00:48:47.914
Let's try and pull it out.

00:48:47.974 --> 00:48:52.623
They slowly pulled it out and looked at the name on the tombstone.

00:48:52.683 --> 00:49:03.964
Well, it's difficult to read, but I think it says Juan Martinez, 1570-1605.

00:49:04.024 --> 00:49:05.214
Said Mike.

00:49:05.274 --> 00:49:08.638
It's the name of the sea captain the pirates killed.

00:49:08.698 --> 00:49:10.369
Said Carlos excitedly.

00:49:10.429 --> 00:49:13.171
He was Isabella Estrada's husband.

00:49:13.231 --> 00:49:16.544
Could Captain Salamanca's treasure be here?

00:49:16.604 --> 00:49:18.395
What do you mean?

00:49:18.455 --> 00:49:19.839
Asked Kate.

00:49:19.899 --> 00:49:22.632
This is where Juan Martinez is buried.

00:49:22.692 --> 00:49:24.683
Yes, cried Carlos.

00:49:24.743 --> 00:49:27.294
It's the perfect hiding place.

00:49:27.354 --> 00:49:30.454
There's only one way to find out, said Mike.

00:49:30.514 --> 00:49:32.415
We have to dig.

00:49:32.475 --> 00:49:34.065
Aren't you afraid?

00:49:34.125 --> 00:49:35.395
Asked Kate.

00:49:35.455 --> 00:49:37.396
Isn't it bad luck?

00:49:37.456 --> 00:49:41.556
I just want to dig under the tombstone, said Mike.

00:49:41.616 --> 00:49:44.117
But we don't have a spade.

00:49:44.177 --> 00:49:46.038
Said Carlos.

00:49:46.098 --> 00:49:49.657
The three friends were silent for a moment.

00:49:49.717 --> 00:49:52.967
You know, said Kate.

00:49:53.027 --> 00:49:55.758
Dad has two spades on the boat.

00:49:55.818 --> 00:49:58.198
He uses them for his work.

00:49:58.258 --> 00:50:02.840
That means we have to tell mom and dad, said Mike.

00:50:02.900 --> 00:50:04.600
I think so.

00:50:04.660 --> 00:50:05.861
Said Kate.

00:50:05.921 --> 00:50:07.851
I'm sure they'll help us.

00:50:07.912 --> 00:50:09.372
They always do.

00:50:09.432 --> 00:50:11.772
We can tell them at dinner.

00:50:11.832 --> 00:50:18.891
That evening at dinner, Kate, Mike, and Carlos told Mr. and Mrs. Sullivan the whole story.

00:50:18.952 --> 00:50:24.112
They stopped eating and were very surprised, but they were not angry.

00:50:24.172 --> 00:50:27.123
They decided to help the three friends.

00:50:27.184 --> 00:50:31.686
This is an exciting adventure, said Mrs. Sullivan.

00:50:31.746 --> 00:50:34.638
And you guys are very good detectives.

00:50:34.698 --> 00:50:36.330
We'll help you.

00:50:36.390 --> 00:50:42.984
If you find the treasure, we'll have to call the California Archaeological Society, said Mr. Sullivan.

00:50:43.044 --> 00:50:52.777
Because the treasure belongs to the state of California, Moral morning, we'll go to the old Spanish lighthouse and start digging.

00:50:52.837 --> 00:50:55.418
Who knows what we'll find?

00:50:55.478 --> 00:51:00.249
By ten o'clock the next morning, they were at the old Spanish lighthouse.

00:51:00.309 --> 00:51:05.190
Mr. Sullivan gave Mike and Carlos two spades and they started digging.

00:51:05.250 --> 00:51:10.951
They dug for a short time, and suddenly, Carlos's spade hit something hard.

00:51:11.011 --> 00:51:13.632
He stopped digging and looked at Mike.

00:51:13.692 --> 00:51:15.133
I found something!

00:51:15.193 --> 00:51:16.284
cried Carlos.

00:51:16.344 --> 00:51:17.515
Let me help you!

00:51:17.575 --> 00:51:19.266
said Mr. Sullivan.

00:51:19.326 --> 00:51:23.310
They pulled a small wooden treasure chest out of the ground.

00:51:23.370 --> 00:51:24.822
It was heavy.

00:51:24.882 --> 00:51:26.503
Wow!

00:51:26.563 --> 00:51:28.985
said Kate and Mrs. Sullivan looking at it.

00:51:29.045 --> 00:51:31.117
This is hard to believe!

00:51:31.177 --> 00:51:32.478
said Mr. Sullivan.

00:51:32.538 --> 00:51:33.879
Can we open it?

00:51:33.939 --> 00:51:34.930
asked Mike.

00:51:34.990 --> 00:51:36.552
Yes, of course!

00:51:36.612 --> 00:51:37.792
said Mr. Sullivan.

00:51:37.852 --> 00:51:39.720
Let's see what's inside.

00:51:39.780 --> 00:51:45.549
The lock was broken, and Carlos and Mike slowly opened the treasure chest.

00:51:45.609 --> 00:51:52.813
It was full of gold and silver coins, jewelry, pearls, and a king's crown.

00:51:52.873 --> 00:51:55.094
Wow!

00:51:55.154 --> 00:51:56.515
They all cried.

00:51:56.575 --> 00:51:58.806
They couldn't believe their eyes.

00:51:58.866 --> 00:52:01.998
Look at all of these gold and silver coins!

00:52:02.058 --> 00:52:03.499
Cried Kate.

00:52:03.559 --> 00:52:08.896
Everyone stared at the treasure in silence, but no one touched it.

00:52:08.956 --> 00:52:13.673
The pirate probably hid this treasure here in the 1600s.

00:52:13.733 --> 00:52:14.914
Said Carlos.

00:52:14.974 --> 00:52:19.268
Another pirate knew about it and planned to come here and dig up the treasure.

00:52:19.328 --> 00:52:21.450
Yeah, said Mike.

00:52:21.510 --> 00:52:25.754
And someone killed him because he didn't want to tell his secret.

00:52:25.814 --> 00:52:30.098
But he wrote his secret on a piece of paper and put it in his hat.

00:52:30.158 --> 00:52:31.208
Said Kate.

00:52:31.268 --> 00:52:34.413
And we found it after 400 years.

00:52:34.474 --> 00:52:38.497
Why did Captain Salamanca have the treasure map?

00:52:38.557 --> 00:52:39.708
Asked Carlos.

00:52:39.768 --> 00:52:41.358
That's a mystery.

00:52:41.418 --> 00:52:43.059
Said Mike smiling.

00:52:43.119 --> 00:52:45.550
What an exciting story.

00:52:45.610 --> 00:52:46.910
Said Mrs. Sullivan.

00:52:46.970 --> 00:52:50.572
Captain Salamanca's treasure map brought you good luck.

00:52:50.632 --> 00:52:54.173
People don't find treasures every day in California.

00:52:54.233 --> 00:52:55.644
Said Mr. Sullivan.

00:52:55.704 --> 00:53:00.736
Now, I'm going to call the California Archaeological Society in San Francisco.

00:53:00.796 --> 00:53:04.230
They'll be very surprised and happy.

00:53:04.290 --> 00:53:06.753
What's going to happen to the treasure?"

00:53:06.813 --> 00:53:08.114
asked Mike.

00:53:08.174 --> 00:53:11.384
Archeologists will study the treasure first.

00:53:11.444 --> 00:53:12.884
Said Mr. Sullivan.

00:53:12.944 --> 00:53:17.095
And then they'll probably take it to one of the Californian museums.

00:53:17.155 --> 00:53:20.476
Journalists may want to write about you in the newspaper.

00:53:20.536 --> 00:53:22.836
Our names in the newspaper?

00:53:22.896 --> 00:53:24.246
Said Kate Happily.

00:53:24.306 --> 00:53:25.737
That's exciting.

00:53:25.797 --> 00:53:27.037
Of course.

00:53:27.097 --> 00:53:28.427
Said Mrs. Sullivan.

00:53:28.487 --> 00:53:33.046
Your adventure will be in all the papers and maybe on TV.

00:53:33.107 --> 00:53:37.510
We're proud of you," said Mr. Sullivan, smiling.

00:53:37.570 --> 00:53:39.634
And of you too, Lucky.

00:53:39.694 --> 00:53:46.272
Lucky barked happily, and ran around the treasure chest.

00:53:46.332 --> 00:53:54.854
Everyone laughed, and Mrs. Sullivan said, well, you didn't get bored on this vacation.

00:53:54.915 --> 00:53:58.550
The three friends said, never.

